## Dataset / lexicon provenance (not MIT by default)

Runtime linguistic assets may be derived from multiple sources with their own
licenses. Public release artifacts must exclude any material without clear
redistribution rights.

Typical sources (see docs and scripts for exact usage):

| Source | Role | Notes |
|--------|------|--------|
| Apple Transliteration labels (local/proprietary) | Strong lexicon / integrity eval | Local-only; never redistribute Apple binaries or Marisa dumps |
| AI4Bharat Aksharantar (guj) | Soft roman↔native pairs | CC0 mined pairs; zip not redistributed |
| Dakshina (Gujarati) | Soft pairs + natives | Follow Dakshina license terms |
| aspell-gu / hunspell | Spell-dict floors | Follow package licenses |
| Google i18n wordcounts / Input Tools | Optional natives | Require explicit CLI path; not always redistributable |
| IndicCorp / Indic wordlists | Frequency | Follow source licenses |
| Wiktionary / Wikipedia extracts | Frequency / wiki floors | CC BY-SA where applicable |

Soft-fill never overrides Apple-strong keys (weight ≥ 100).
Aksharantar soft entries do not auto-join `attested.json`.

